Make qubes.WaitForNetworkUplink work without systemd, fast-path when already up,
and actively (re)configure the uplink only when needed on a deferred/paused
netvm change.

dom0 (qubes-core-admin apply_deferred_netvm) invokes this qrexec service after a
deferred/paused netvm change, wrapped in asyncio.wait_for(..., timeout=10).  On
domain-unpaused that 10s window also has to absorb qrexec/vchan re-establishment
to the just-unpaused VM, so the guest side must spend as little time as possible.

Upstream polls `systemctl is-active qubes-network-uplink@<iface>.service` -- a
unit whose ExecStart is `setup-ip add`, so polling implicitly drives
reconfiguration (the matching udev rule does `systemctl restart` of that unit on
vif add).  On a native Guix template using the Shepherd there is no systemd, no
systemctl, and no per-interface uplink unit; and a netvm pause/unpause does not
necessarily remove and re-add the AppVM frontend interface, so the vif-hotplug
udev rule (which runs `herd reconfigure qubes-network-uplink <iface>') may not
fire.  When systemctl is absent:
  1. fast path: if the managed interface is already carrier/LOWER_UP, exit 0
     immediately (do not spend the dom0 budget on a needless reconfigure);
  2. otherwise actively run `herd reconfigure qubes-network-uplink <iface>`
     (idempotent, serialized by Shepherd) with a tight 3s bound, then poll
     briefly for readiness -- total guest-side time stays well under dom0's 10s.

systemd distributions are unaffected: systemctl is present, so the original
`systemctl is-active` poll runs unchanged.

Upstream: QubesOS/qubes-core-agent-linux, qubes-rpc/qubes.WaitForNetworkUplink.
Status: should-upstream (portable; adds a fast Shepherd-driven path for systemd-less VMs).
diff --git a/qubes-rpc/qubes.WaitForNetworkUplink b/qubes-rpc/qubes.WaitForNetworkUplink
index 359ee32..ee0b9af 100644
--- a/qubes-rpc/qubes.WaitForNetworkUplink
+++ b/qubes-rpc/qubes.WaitForNetworkUplink
@@ -9,13 +9,51 @@ if test -z "$iface"; then
   exit
 fi
 
-i=0
-while test $i -le 10; do
-  if systemctl is-active --quiet "qubes-network-uplink@$iface.service"; then
-    ip link show "$iface" | grep "state UP" || exit 4
+if command -v systemctl >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+  # systemd: poll the per-interface uplink unit (its ExecStart runs setup-ip).
+  i=0
+  while test $i -le 10; do
+    if systemctl is-active --quiet "qubes-network-uplink@$iface.service"; then
+      ip link show "$iface" | grep "state UP" || exit 4
+      exit 0
+    fi
+    sleep 0.3
+    i=$((i+1))
+  done
+  exit 3
+else
+  # No systemd (native Guix template using the Shepherd): there is no
+  # qubes-network-uplink@<iface> unit whose start runs setup-ip.  dom0 invokes
+  # this service from apply_deferred_netvm() and waits at most ~10s for the WHOLE
+  # qrexec call -- which, on domain-unpaused, also includes qrexec/vchan
+  # re-establishment to the just-unpaused VM.  So minimise guest-side latency:
+  # check readiness FIRST and exit immediately if the link is already usable;
+  # only repair (drive a Shepherd reconfigure) when it is not, then poll briefly.
+  # A netvm pause/unpause does not necessarily re-add the AppVM frontend
+  # interface, so the vif-hotplug udev rule (which runs `herd reconfigure') may
+  # not fire -- hence the active repair when needed.
+  uplink_ready() {
+    [ -d "/sys/class/net/$iface" ] || return 1
+    if [ -r "/sys/class/net/$iface/carrier" ] &&
+       [ "$(cat "/sys/class/net/$iface/carrier" 2>/dev/null)" = 1 ]; then
+      return 0
+    fi
+    ip link show dev "$iface" 2>/dev/null | grep -q "LOWER_UP"
+  }
+  # Fast path: already usable after resume -> succeed without touching Shepherd.
+  if uplink_ready; then
     exit 0
   fi
-  sleep 0.3
-  i=$((i+1))
-done
-exit 3
+  # Repair only when needed, with a tight bound, leaving margin under dom0's 10s.
+  herd=/run/current-system/profile/bin/herd
+  timeout 3 "$herd" reconfigure qubes-network-uplink "$iface" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
+  i=0
+  while test $i -le 12; do
+    if uplink_ready; then
+      exit 0
+    fi
+    sleep 0.25
+    i=$((i+1))
+  done
+  exit 3
+fi
